<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liaquat Ali Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1895–1951</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liaquat Ali Khan was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/all-india-muslim-league">All-India Muslim League</a> and close associate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-jinnah">Muhammad Ali Jinnah</a> who became the first prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> in 1947. He led the new state through partition, the refugee crisis and the first war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>, and moved the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/objectives-resolution">Objectives Resolution</a> of 1949 on the constitution. He was assassinated in Rawalpindi in October 1951.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liaquat-ali-khan.jpg" alt="Liaquat Ali Khan" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author - but due to age, image in public domain · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liaquat_Ali_Khan_1945.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
